Switch: sqlite caches without a journal file, rebuilt when they cannot be opened

On the console both caches (dawn_cache.db and pipeline_cache.db on the SD card) failed
their first transaction with "database disk image is malformed" on every run, even
after the files were deleted, so every shader and pipeline was compiled again each run.

On Horizon the caches now use journal_mode=MEMORY and synchronous=OFF instead of WAL
(compiled out there) and NORMAL: no rollback journal file is created, stat'ed or
unlinked next to the database, and nothing waits for the card. A cache that still
cannot be opened is removed (with any journal left next to it) and created once more
from an empty file; the log says so with the old file's size. The sqlite build adds
exclusive locking and in-memory temp files, and its error log goes to the run log
(switch/aurora/sqlite_horizon.c), which names the exact check that fails if this does
not cure it.

Switch only (switch/native/aurora/patches); not for upstream.

